  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 125 PM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nThe upper-level ridge builds back over the Great Plains this \nweekend, with its southwestern edge holding its grip on our area. \nThis yields afternoon highs in the upper 90s across much of the \nregion Saturday, with triple digit heat confined to the Pecos \nRiver/Rio Grande Valleys and northeast portions of the Permian \nBasin. The good news is Saturday looks to be the last day of \nwidespread triple digit heat. By early next week, the upper ridge \nslowly moves east towards the southeastern CONUS. Decreasing \nthicknesses will allow for tempertures to gradually cool a degree \nalmost daily next week. Increasing Gulf moisture overrunning \nsoutheasterly upslope flow yields daily chances of convection across \nthe western higher terrain. The best chances (20-40%) remain \nconfined to the Davis Mountains and surrounding areas. However, it's \nnot out of the realm of possibility that convective development \ncould spread eastward mid-to-late next week. We will continue to \nmonitor trends and refine the forecast as new data warrants it.\n  \nGreening",
